Proposed patch (NOT applied). src/gpuf/methods/analog.py lines 121-126, AnalogTable.__init__.
Problem: a series is dropped from the whole table when it has < 2 rows or any non-positive value over the
table's full span (cap). At a validation origin, a series with one row on or before the origin enters the
standardisation sums (AnalogTable.sd) only if it has more rows after the origin, so forecasts depend on the
existence of post-origin rows. Verified fix: experiments/audit/analog_fix.py (deletion and wild tests
bit-identical after the patch; shipped vs patched at the 18 validation origins differ by at most 2.1e-5 in log).

--- a/src/gpuf/methods/analog.py
+++ b/src/gpuf/methods/analog.py
@@ -120,10 +120,12 @@ class AnalogTable:
         for sid, g in df.groupby("series_id", sort=True):
             g = g.sort_values("day")
+            g = g[g["value"] > 0]  # drop bad rows one by one; never the whole series on a later row
+            if len(g) == 0:
+                continue
             days = g["day"].to_numpy(np.int64)
             vals = g["value"].to_numpy(np.float64)
-            if len(days) < 2 or not (vals > 0).all():
-                continue
             npv = np.nan_to_num(g["n_providers"].to_numpy(np.float64), nan=1.0)
             F = _series_features(days, vals, npv)
